1. CRITICAL AUTHENTICATION AND ONBOARDING FIX
Current problem

The application sometimes asks users to complete onboarding repeatedly, including after signup, login, or returning to an already authenticated session.

This must be fixed permanently.
Required authentication behavior

Implement the following flow:

    A new visitor opens Healno and sees the landing page or authentication screen, depending on the existing product flow.

    A new user signs up and verifies their account if verification is required by the existing authentication system.

    After successful signup, the user completes onboarding once.

    Their onboarding answers and completion status are saved securely against their authenticated user ID.

    After completion, the user is redirected directly to the application dashboard.

    When that user logs out and logs back in later, they must go directly to the app, not the landing page or onboarding.

    If a user has partially completed onboarding and returns later, resume the incomplete steps using their saved progress.

    If onboarding is complete, never show it again automatically.

    If the user explicitly chooses to edit their information, open the relevant profile or health settings instead of restarting onboarding.

    If the session expires, handle authentication safely and redirect the user to sign in. After successful authentication, restore the correct destination.

Technical implementation

    Inspect the current authentication provider, session handling, routing, and database before implementing changes.

    Use the authenticated user ID as the source of truth.

    Store onboarding completion status and progress persistently in the database.

    Do not rely exclusively on browser state, local storage, or session storage to determine completion.

    Load the authenticated user's profile and onboarding status before deciding which page to display.

    Prevent duplicate onboarding submissions and duplicate profile records.

    Add appropriate route guards for public pages, onboarding, and authenticated application routes.

    Handle refreshes, multiple tabs, slow API responses, expired sessions, and returning users correctly.

    Prevent redirect loops and flashes of the wrong page.

    Keep the session secure using the existing authentication provider's recommended approach.

Expected routing behavior
User state	Required destination
Not authenticated	Landing page or login/signup
Newly registered, onboarding incomplete	Onboarding
Returning user, onboarding incomplete	Resume onboarding
Returning user, onboarding complete	Home dashboard
Authenticated user opening the public landing page	Redirect to the app dashboard
Authenticated user editing profile information	Profile/settings, not onboarding
User logs out	Public landing or login page

Do not mark onboarding complete until the required steps have been saved successfully.
